* Demand (measured)

Found by the demand scan of vla-entity-property-table-on-demand
(.vla-demand.py, 1416 AutoLISP files): code that runs today calls COM
properties of the APPLICATION / DOCUMENT objects that cador does not have:

  ActiveDocument (9 calls, has)   SupportPath (7)   Application (3)
  Preferences (3)   Layers (2, has)   Layouts (2)   Blocks (2, has)
  Files (2)   ActiveProfile (1)   Profiles (1)   Documents (1, has)
  Active (1)

Callers: EPUREE (src/comu.lsp -- epuree:delete-layout-by-name-safe walks
vla-get-layouts / vla-item by name; a Documents walk tests vla-get-Active)
and its SNCF upstream (SNCF_startup.lsp reads and sets
Preferences -> Files -> SupportPath, reads Profiles / ActiveProfile).

* To do (per the vla-entity-property-table-on-demand discipline)

For each: classify against both vendors first (AGENTS.md, dialect
divergence), probe what the vendor returns, then implement with a test:
  - Document.Layouts collection + Item by name (needs layouts in the
    headless model -- shared with alref's CHSPACE);
  - Document.Active (T for the active document of the Documents
    collection);
  - Preferences -> Files -> SupportPath (the ACAD support path string --
    which host value backs it: (getenv "ACAD"), SRCHPATH?) and its setter;
  - Preferences -> Profiles -> ActiveProfile.
